      "description": "* Architected and led the development of an agentic AI platform for scalable, domain-specific knowledge base construction supporting Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). Directed the integration of custom agents to automate complex workflows and domain-specific tasks, including silicon validation and QA test plan generation, self-help support for enterprise codebases and workflows across 200k+ LOC, and achieving a 90% accuracy rate on process design data queries—outperforming existing solutions by 50%. (LLM, NLP, ChromaDb, Visual Studio Code, GitHub Copilot, Python, Typescript).\n\n  * Architected and implemented CI/CD infrastructure for test automation (PyTest). Deployed on distributed high-performance computing (HPC) heterogeneous clusters, optimizing resource utilization, scalability, and reliability. Achieved over a 1000x increase in test case capacity and reduced cycle time by 2x. Improved compute efficiency by 4x and reduced resource usage per release by 12%. Increased system stability, lowering failure rates from 5% to ≤0.001% per run. (Python, Ruby, ELK Stack, ElasticSearch, Jira, GitHub, GitLab, Jenkins, VS Code, HPC, Kubernetes, Docker/Singularity, REST API).\n\n  * Led a department-wide effort to automate existing workflows, doubling development and validation efficiency, and completing 25+ automation projects, saving 14 weeks of turnaround time. (Python, Perl, Value Stream Mapping [VSM], Interaction Design)\n\n  * Automated software development processes and methodologies, improving efficiency and quality. (GitLab, GitHub, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, mypy, pylint)\n\n  * Architected Intel’s unified infrastructure for extraction flow validation, supporting all internal and IDM 2.0 external customers.\n\n  * Directed the development of advanced silicon validation tools, establishing Intel Design for Test (DFT) and diagnostics standards. (C++, Visual Basic, Interaction/Visual Design)",
